                <pb facs="0936" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.602/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-11T17:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 12—3:47
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Reliably informed that Costa Rican Congress this afternoon passed the law
                    annulling Tinoco contracts, etc., referred to in last paragraph my August 3, 1
                    p.m. over the veto by more than two thirds. This includes Amory concession.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
